WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:08.000
How attention moves information between tokens.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Every dot is one number this small model computed: 1,048,576 of them.

3
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:21.000
This is one sequence it read: 64 positions, 64 numbers each.

4
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.000
The sequence is 64 random characters. One stretch of them repeats.

5
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Outside the repeat the model gets 1.7% of next characters right, about chance. Inside it, 95.8%.

6
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.000
First, a head in layer 0 moves each character one position forward.

7
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:46.000
It puts 0.51 of its attention on the previous token. Switch it off and repeat accuracy falls to 7.9%.

8
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:51.000
Then layer 1 looks for the earlier copy of the current character.

9
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:55.000
It attends to the character that came after that copy, and that is the prediction.

10
00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:01.000
Switch off both layer 1 heads and repeat accuracy falls to 1.7%.

11
00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:07.000
Two steps: copy the previous character forward, then match it to find what came next.

12
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:13.000
Every number here was read from the model's output file while the film was drawn.
